AUN Filestore - phar distribution
=================================


About
-----

AUN Filestore is an Econet fileserver implementation (using AUN) for Linux and
other platforms. It is written in PHP and provides file and print services to
Acorn RISC machines and emulated BBCs, on top of a layer 2 emulation of Econet.

This distribution bundles the whole server - all of the PHP code and its
Composer dependencies - into a single archive, filestore.phar, together with a
couple of sample config files and two empty working directories.


Requirements
------------

* PHP 8.4 or newer on the PATH, with the pcntl, sockets, pdo and phar
  extensions enabled.


Layout
------

    filestore.phar    the server
    run.sh            convenience launcher (runs the server in the foreground)
    default.conf      sample configuration - edit to taste
    users.txt         sample user database (user: SYST, password: SYST)
    file-root/        the root of the virtual econet filesystem
    print-spool/      spooled print jobs land here


Running
-------

From inside this directory:

    ./run.sh

or, to run it in the background:

    php filestore.phar -c . -d -p filestored.pid

The `-c` option points at the directory holding the *.conf file(s).


Admin web interface
-------------------

The server starts a browser based admin interface on the address and port set by
`webadmin_listen_address` / `webadmin_listen_port` in default.conf (0.0.0.0:8080
by default), e.g. http://localhost:8080/ .
